# K03 NS-ROLES-1b (Codex K03-S5-ALIAS-VISIBILITY-20261007-07 Q1, K03-NS-ROLES-NEXT-20261007-09; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md
# :666, :722): for absent b, `b: tick` with tick a method binds b to tick's whole occurrence -- no wrapper, nothing
# runs at the binding; `b: args` and `b(args)` call tick, with its signature, on the occurrence b holds.
# The binding named alone is the method's call with no actuals, as the method's name is: c as a value gives two's
# result, `c` and `c()` as statements call two.  Exit 7; 81 if the binding ran two, 82/83 otherwise.
int: ticks 0
fn: two () int
    node\ticks: node\ticks + 10
    return: 2
end: two
fn: m () int
    c: two
    if: node\ticks != 0
        return: 81
    if: c != 2
        return: 82
    c
    c()
    if: node\ticks != 30
        return: 83
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
